ot promise exclusive ownership of licensed or generated material.","overlap":"Choose one production plan per site. Production-only is available for a healthy supported site with maintenance handled elsewhere. Brochure Care adds $100/month; Commerce replaces it for another $146/month. Never bill both Care variants or a second standalone Care fee.","onboarding":"Care onboarding is $195 for Brochure or $395 for Commerce. It is waived immediately after a W&M build with the same complete handoff, and for the first three approved introductory monthly production clients who select Care. Standalone Care retains its onboarding fee. The full compatibility, access, monitoring and recovery checks still apply. Production-only plans have no Care onboarding charge; a pre-start fit and access review is included. Any remediation is agreed separately before acceptance. Eligibility and the exact first invoice are confirmed before payment.","measurement":"The first paid production cycle includes missing supported native GA4 and Search Console setup plus one inquiry-success event, using client-approved consent settings. Working measurement is reused. There is no separate fee for this basic setup; advanced tagging or dashboards need an incremental quote. If native setup is unavailable, agree an equivalent or revised scope before payment. The cycle still includes all promised production outputs."},"required_facts":["business_identity","service_goals","approved_claims","primary_contact"],"required_access":[]}'::jsonb)) seed(s);
insert into wm.catalog_registry(catalog_id,variant,catalog_version,snapshot,digest) select s->>'id',s->>'variant',s->>'catalog_version',s,wm.hash_json(s) from (values('{"schema":1,"id":"workflow","variant":"standard","name":"Workflow Automation Sprint","service_type":"catalog_project","catalog_version":"2026-10-29-v4-offers","currency":"USD","scope":"Choose one route before booking: up to five distinct simple native automations for one related business process, OR one more complex workflow matching the separate advanced route. The routes do not stack. Simple route: up to three existing tools across the whole package. Each automation has one genuine trigger-to-outcome purpose, up to three action steps, one conditional branch and eight mapped fields. Aggregate maximum: five triggers, fifteen actions, five branches and forty mapped fields. Do not relabel sequential steps of one workflow as separate automations. Use supported native connectors in client-owned accounts. No custom API connector, historic migration, bidirectional synchronization or unsupported authentication in the simple route. Confirm connector actions and subscription limits before accepting the fee. Map each automation and define success, duplicates and failures. Configure required-data validation, duplicate protection where stable identifiers permit it, one common failure-notification destination, native run history and a documented manual fallback. For every automation, run at least five agreed cases: normal, missing/invalid input, duplicate, provider failure and retry/recovery. Record limitations and obtain explicit acceptance before live activation. One consolidated review, workflow diagrams, connection inventory and written/recorded operator training. Optional 60-minute training substitutes for the written exchange. Client owns accounts and pays disclosed task/app usage. Read-only operational checks around day 7 and day 14, plus 30 calendar days to report W&M-caused defects. No continuous human monitoring or unlimited changes. Fixing an unchanged accepted deliverable is owed even if its estimate overruns.","exclusions":["Unbounded API development, legacy systems, bespoke authentication or complex data reconciliation","Financial decisions, medical/legal decision automation, payroll or automated irreversible account changes","Ongoing campaign management, bulk outreach or unattended AI decisions with material consequences"],"acceptance":["Each agreed trigger-to-outcome automation passes its five documented success/failure tests.","The operator can inspect run history, receive the failure notification and follow the manual fallback.","Client-approved access, usage costs, data mapping, rollback/disable steps and ownership are documented.","All agreed automations are delivered; a count is not inflated by counting individual actions as separate workflows."],"components":[],"milestones":[{"id":"stage_1","deliverable":"Book the agreed scope","amount_minor":74750,"acceptance_rule":"Book the agreed scope","proof":"booking"},{"id":"stage_2","deliverable":"Accept the agreed deliverables","amount_minor":74750,"acceptance_rule":"Accept the agreed deliverables","proof":"approved_work"}],"entitlements":[],"quote_required":false,"hosting_offset_cap_minor":0,"terms":{"delivery":"Delivery begins at your ready, booked start: approved scope, initial payment, access and business facts in place. The next available start is confirmed separately. Normal review time is included; allow two business days for consolidated feedback at each gate. The shortest targets need prompt approvals. Missing inputs or approved changes can move dates. Written communication is standard; calls are optional.","payment":"Book the agreed scope: 747.50 USD; Accept the agreed deliverables: 747.50 USD","cancellation":"Use a written reconciliation: pay for completed agreed work and approved nonrecoverable external expenses; return unearned prepaid fees. Define the reconciliation and payment timetable in the pr